title: Before Warsaw
subtitle: The Red Army is at the gates of the Polish capital.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 8 and crisis = 0 and ending_id = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3

= Before Warsaw

In the second week of August the Red Army reaches the Vistula. Its cavalry is across the river north of Warsaw, and its patrols ride along the East Prussian border. In Białystok a Polish Revolutionary Committee under Julian Marchlewski waits to take power. [? if border_rising = 1 : Our districts in the east are ready. ?]

- @danzig: Send our best people to the Danzig docks.
- @strike: Call a general strike for Soviet Russia.

@danzig
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Every ship left in the harbour is a battery that never fires.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; warsaw_bonus += 1
go-to: battle

@strike
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Few will come out, and the police are waiting.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.warsaw_bonus += 1;
Q.repression += 6;
Q.worker_support -= 2;
!}
go-to: battle

@battle
title: The Battle of Warsaw
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
var p = 0.04 + 0.04 * Q.warsaw_bonus + Math.max(0, Q.world_revolution - 60) / 400;
Q.warsaw_outcome = Math.random() < p ? 2 : 1;
if (Q.warsaw_outcome == 2) {
    Q.world_revolution += 20;
    Q.soviet_russia_status = 'The Red Army has taken Warsaw';
    Q.stability -= 8;
    Q.militancy += 8;
    RG.news('The Red Army enters Warsaw', 3);
    RG.ecci('all', 5);
    RG.ledger('The Red Army took Warsaw in August 1920.', 'e20_warsaw');
} else {
    Q.world_revolution -= 10;
    Q.soviet_russia_status = 'The civil war is won; the Red Army was stopped at Warsaw';
    Q.stability += 3;
    RG.news('Miracle on the Vistula: the Red Army routed before Warsaw', 3);
}
!}

= The Battle of Warsaw

[? if warsaw_outcome = 1 : On 16 August Piłsudski strikes from the south into the Red Army's open flank. In ten days Tukhachevsky's armies are routed, and whole divisions flee into East Prussia, where they are interned. The Poles call it the miracle on the Vistula. ?]

[? if warsaw_outcome = 2 : Piłsudski's counter-attack from the Wieprz comes too late and too weak. On 19 August the Red Army enters Warsaw, and Marchlewski proclaims a Polish Soviet Republic from the Royal Castle. The revolution has a common border with Germany. ?]
